From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:57:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(connection): detect Bedrock servers in version
 auto-detect

ViaFabricPlus detects a server's version with a Java status request over
TCP. A Bedrock server never answers that request, so an entry on auto
detect joined as Java and timed out on the HTTP NetherNet signaling port.

Before the Java request, query the HTTP NetherNet capability endpoint
(GET /v1/join), which native clients query before every join. A 2xx answer
selects Bedrock. Java servers close the connection on the HTTP request,
so detection falls through to the Java request without a long wait.
Explicit nethernet:// addresses select Bedrock without a request.

The probe uses plain HTTP, like the server list status ping, and a
three-second limit so an unresponsive port cannot stall the join screen.

